CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ defaulted copy constructor: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^PARSING ERROR$
--
`= default' and `= delete' were a parse error before C++11, so with libc++
(`exception(const exception &) _NOEXCEPT = default;') every C++98 program
including a standard header failed to parse.
